# Brand-guide and component-sheet build output. The .py and .tex sources beside these are
# committed; the rendered PDF is regenerated by `python3 brand_guide.py` / `components.py`
# and must not be. These rules live in the ROOT .gitignore — which ships and stays
# `copier update`-able — rather than in a template-only nested file, because a generated
# project running either build hits exactly the same problem on day one.
#
# xelatex is invoked with -output-directory pointing at a temp dir and only the PDF is moved
# into the tree, so there is normally no .aux/.log litter; the aux patterns cover a manual
# xelatex run in that directory.
project-management/src/06-BRAND-GUIDE/guide-build/*.pdf
project-management/src/07-COMPONENTS/component-build/*.pdf
project-management/src/06-BRAND-GUIDE/guide-build/*.aux
project-management/src/06-BRAND-GUIDE/guide-build/*.log
project-management/src/06-BRAND-GUIDE/guide-build/*.out
project-management/src/07-COMPONENTS/component-build/*.aux
project-management/src/07-COMPONENTS/component-build/*.log
project-management/src/07-COMPONENTS/component-build/*.out

# Docker
*.override.yml

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml

# Celery beat PersistentScheduler state (runtime DB — redirected to /tmp in compose;
# this guards against a stray run writing it into the bind-mounted repo working tree)
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat-schedule*

# Claude Code agent worktrees (nested git repos — never commit)
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/token.md

# Added by code-review-graph
.code-review-graph/

# code-review-graph install generates AI-assistant rule files at the repo root. This project is
# Claude Code only (its manual is .claude/CLAUDE.md), so keep the generated duplicates out of the
# repo — they regenerate on `code-review-graph install`. Leading slashes anchor to root, so
# .claude/CLAUDE.md, code/CLAUDE.md, etc. are unaffected.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/GEMINI.md
/.cursorrules
/.windsurfrules
/.kiro/

# Keep Claude Plugins
!.claude/plugins/
